{"id": "one-owner-several-names", "title": "One owner, several names: orders under two names in the same fortnight", "seconds": 130.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:exurTFaGNF2gnRcPNH8I", "narrator": "Phil", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "cbda71480eac6263", "words": 404, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Can one owner hide behind two business names, to win more City work? That’s what we checked.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.0, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "question", "name": "One owner", "sub": ""}, {"art": "contract", "name": "First business name", "sub": ""}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Second business name", "sub": ""}], "kicker": "The question"}, "emph": ["two business names"], "wt": [0.11, 0.2, 0.46, 0.8, 1.11, 1.4, 1.64, 2.06, 2.47, 2.6, 2.84, 3.05, 3.32, 3.73, 4.09, 4.21, 4.38]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "story[2]"], "text": "How many sets of City payees trace back to one owner, on the record?", "t0": 5.12, "t1": 8.58, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Owner-groups on record", "sub": "registry, licences, tax returns"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.32, 0.56, 0.65, 0.92, 1.38, 1.63, 1.8, 1.98, 2.19, 2.62, 2.83, 2.98]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["story[2]", "suspicious[1]"], "text": "The answer: 101 owner-groups with two or more payee names.", "t0": 8.58, "t1": 13.4, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "101", "label": "owner-groups with two or more payee names"}, "emph": ["101"], "wt": [0.04, 0.6, 1.51, 1.65, 1.99, 2.17, 2.33, 3.17, 3.32, 3.54, 3.71, 3.96, 4.41]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "Each one is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 13.92, "t1": 15.91, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.32, 0.46, 0.56, 1.17, 1.27, 1.37]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The ties come from the City’s registry, State licences and the groups’ own filings.", "t0": 16.13, "t1": 20.06, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "What the records show", "sub": "City business registry, State contractor licences, tax returns"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.36, 0.55, 0.67, 0.77, 1.11, 1.65, 2.05, 2.57, 2.74, 2.83, 3.17, 3.39]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Then the bids. On 108 bid lists, no two bidders tie back to one owner.", "t0": 20.18, "t1": 25.45, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Bid lists checked", "rows": [["Bid lists", "108"], ["Bidder names", "121"], ["Found in the City registry", "90"]]}, "emph": ["no two bidders"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.36, 1.22, 1.5, 1.63, 1.89, 2.08, 2.39, 2.96, 3.18, 3.4, 3.87, 4.11, 4.31, 4.47, 4.72]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The first lead is small orders.", "t0": 25.67, "t1": 27.37, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Small orders, two sister names", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.34, 0.59, 0.84, 1.28]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "A department can approve an order alone, if it’s under a limit.", "t0": 27.49, "t1": 30.09, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Small orders, two sister names", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.03, 0.43, 0.56, 0.82, 0.92, 1.25, 1.71, 1.82, 1.96, 2.16, 2.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Two orders, to two names of one owner, days apart. Each is under. Together, some are over.", "t0": 30.21, "t1": 35.42, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "Order to name one", "sub": "under the limit"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Order to name two", "sub": "under the limit"}, {"art": "question", "name": "Together", "sub": "over it?"}], "kicker": "The first lead"}, "emph": ["Together"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.6, 0.78, 0.98, 1.27, 1.45, 1.64, 2.12, 2.39, 2.83, 3.27, 3.44, 3.93, 4.33, 4.63, 4.8]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "We tested 69,068 small orders. The pattern showed up 19 times, in 5 pairs.", "t0": 35.54, "t1": 41.15, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "19", "label": "times, across 5 department-and-vendor pairs"}, "emph": ["19 times"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.51, 0.97, 1.34, 1.94, 2.4, 2.93, 3.17, 3.49, 3.73, 3.9, 4.27, 4.69, 4.8, 5.13]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Most often: Ferguson Enterprises and Ferguson Waterworks, with the water department. 5 times.", "t0": 41.27, "t1": 45.82, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Ferguson Enterprises Inc. and Ferguson Waterworks", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "with the Public Utilities Commsn"}, "emph": ["5 times"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.59, 1.11, 1.63, 1.78, 2.24, 2.84, 3.02, 3.11, 3.36, 3.91, 4.12]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "innocent[5]"], "text": "But the registry lists Ferguson Waterworks as a Ferguson Enterprises trade name: one company.", "t0": 45.94, "t1": 50.78, "shot": "b10b", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "one company under two names, not two firms"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.16, 0.64, 0.96, 1.42, 2.0, 2.11, 2.22, 2.64, 3.29, 3.57, 4.16, 4.37]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Must sister firms be counted together? The records don’t say.", "t0": 50.9, "t1": 53.91, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Whether related vendors must be counted together is not in the files on disk"}, "wt": [0.03, 0.31, 0.65, 0.95, 1.03, 1.36, 1.88, 2.05, 2.38, 2.68]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead is money.", "t0": 54.13, "t1": 55.66, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Paid under second names", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.41, 0.78, 1.06]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "How much went to the second names, since 2019?", "t0": 55.78, "t1": 58.26, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Paid under second names", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.3, 0.49, 0.56, 0.7, 0.99, 1.43, 1.63, 1.85]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "amount"], "text": "1.23 billion dollars.", "t0": 58.26, "t1": 60.93, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.23 billion", "label": "paid under second and later names since fiscal 2019"}, "emph": ["1.23"], "wt": [0.04, 0.66, 1.02, 1.18, 1.54, 2.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The biggest pair: Mckesson Corporation, 567.5 million dollars.", "t0": 61.45, "t1": 65.97, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Mckesson Corporation", "$567.5 million"], "b": ["Mckesson Plasma and Biologics LLC", "$185.2 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.36, 0.8, 1.35, 2.08, 2.26, 2.5, 3.1, 3.46, 3.62, 4.03]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Its sister firm, 185.2 million.", "t0": 66.09, "t1": 68.69, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Mckesson Corporation", "$567.5 million"], "b": ["Mckesson Plasma and Biologics LLC", "$185.2 million"]}, "emph": ["185.2 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.47, 0.9, 1.03, 1.25, 1.79, 2.08, 2.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Most say so openly. Did a limit or a bid list treat them as two?", "t0": 68.81, "t1": 72.45, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "whether a limit, a bid list or a pool treated the names as separate parties"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.4, 0.56, 1.13, 1.46, 1.54, 1.83, 1.99, 2.08, 2.28, 2.53, 2.73, 2.94, 3.11]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "Then local firms. On 38 contracts,", "t0": 72.45, "t1": 75.03, "shot": "b15b", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "38", "label": "contracts: a certified local subcontractor under its own recorded affiliate"}, "emph": ["38 contracts"], "wt": [0.04, 0.83, 1.11, 1.52, 1.68, 2.04]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "a certified local subcontractor works under its own recorded affiliate.", "t0": 75.03, "t1": 78.57, "shot": "b15c", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Certified local subcontractor", "sub": "working under its own recorded affiliate"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.13, 0.65, 0.92, 1.58, 1.85, 2.11, 2.27, 2.53, 2.99]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[8]"], "text": "One pair: 22 contracts, 5.1 million dollars.", "t0": 78.69, "t1": 81.41, "shot": "b15a", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "ESQUIVEL GRADING & PAVING INC", "sub": "prime contractor"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "LAVINA TRUCKING, INC.", "sub": "local-business subcontractor, its recorded affiliate"}, {"art": "money", "name": "22 contracts", "sub": "$5.1 million"}], "kicker": "Affiliates on one team"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.46, 0.82, 1.39, 1.54, 1.8, 1.93, 2.23]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["notEstablished[4]", "innocent[3]"], "text": "Did that share count toward a local goal? The records don’t show.", "t0": 81.53, "t1": 85.14, "shot": "b15a", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "ESQUIVEL GRADING & PAVING INC", "sub": "prime contractor"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "LAVINA TRUCKING, INC.", "sub": "local-business subcontractor, its recorded affiliate"}, {"art": "money", "name": "22 contracts", "sub": "$5.1 million"}], "kicker": "Affiliates on one team"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.31, 0.58, 0.83, 1.03, 1.11, 1.39, 1.87, 2.33, 2.78, 3.15]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead: work pools.", "t0": 85.36, "t1": 87.03, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "In the same pool twice", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.32, 0.91, 1.14]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "In 3 of 50, a firm has its own place, plus one through a joint team.", "t0": 87.15, "t1": 91.03, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "In the same pool twice", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "emph": ["3 of 50"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.38, 0.51, 0.97, 1.05, 1.3, 1.43, 1.58, 1.79, 2.31, 2.55, 2.83, 3.1, 3.19, 3.52]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Two chances at work meant to be shared. Each pool’s rules decide.", "t0": 91.15, "t1": 94.43, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "two chances at work meant to be shared around"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.43, 0.54, 0.85, 1.09, 1.18, 1.33, 1.8, 2.14, 2.54, 2.94]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead is licences and drawings.", "t0": 94.65, "t1": 96.87, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "292", "label": "taxi medallions held by one name: SFFCU Taxi Medallion Holder"}, "wt": [0.02, 0.08, 0.36, 0.64, 0.83, 1.36, 1.56]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "18 taxi medallion holders hold more than one. The largest holds 292.", "t0": 96.99, "t1": 102.38, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "292", "label": "taxi medallions held by one name: SFFCU Taxi Medallion Holder"}, "emph": ["292"], "wt": [0.0, 0.56, 0.98, 1.45, 1.88, 2.23, 2.37, 2.6, 2.92, 3.14, 3.71, 4.0, 4.23, 4.52]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "17 cannabis owner groups hold licences under two or more names.", "t0": 102.5, "t1": 106.92, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "17", "label": "cannabis owner-groups with licences under two or more names"}, "emph": ["17"], "wt": [0.0, 0.66, 1.18, 1.45, 1.79, 2.07, 2.64, 2.97, 3.36, 3.59, 3.89]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[4]"], "text": "The fifth lead is health providers. One owner group holds 32 provider names, and 96 billing numbers.", "t0": 107.14, "t1": 112.59, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "32", "label": "provider names under one owner group (96 billing numbers)"}, "emph": ["32"], "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.32, 0.6, 0.77, 1.0, 1.67, 2.1, 2.33, 2.64, 2.85, 3.25, 3.66, 4.02, 4.11, 4.64, 4.92]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Separate names at one address can be one business.", "t0": 112.71, "t1": 115.04, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "separate names can be one business"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.64, 0.78, 0.97, 1.31, 1.5, 1.64, 1.84]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The records don’t show any order was split on purpose. And an address alone proves nothing.", "t0": 115.26, "t1": 119.95, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any purchase was split on purpose", "Any tie that rests on an address alone"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.38, 0.6, 0.86, 1.05, 1.33, 1.53, 1.88, 2.07, 2.67, 2.88, 2.99, 3.46, 3.84, 4.18]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[4]"], "text": "What would settle it? State filings naming each firm’s officers, and the bid rules on related firms.", "t0": 120.07, "t1": 125.33, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "State filings naming each firm’s officers"}, {"who": "", "what": "Bid rules on related firms"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.23, 0.56, 0.82, 1.37, 1.83, 2.16, 2.37, 2.71, 3.33, 3.6, 3.7, 3.91, 4.23, 4.37, 4.78]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Nothing here shows a rule was broken.", "t0": 125.45, "t1": 127.64, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.66, 0.97, 1.22, 1.31, 1.56, 1.72]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.76, "t1": 129.75, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.22, 0.37, 0.5, 1.09, 1.27, 1.39]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · small orders", "lead2": "Lead 2 · second names", "lead3": "Lead 3 · pools", "lead4": "Lead 4 · licences", "lead5": "Lead 5 · providers", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "question"}